cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository, please cite both the associated article and this software."
title: "Code for Predicting Olympic Medal Outcomes in 1,011 Elite Athletes Using Multimodal Machine Learning"
type: software

authors:
  - family-names: "Choi"
    given-names: "Hyoungjoo"

repository-code: "https://github.com/hjchoipt-byte/olympic-medal-outcome-ml"

version: "1.0.0"

date-released: "2026-08-02"

abstract: >
  Public reproducibility code accompanying the manuscript
  "Predicting Olympic medal outcomes in 1,011 elite athletes using
  multimodal machine learning". The repository contains the complete
  analysis workflow, including data preprocessing, feature selection,
  SHAP analyses, nested cross-validation, and supplementary analyses.

license: MIT

keywords:
  - machine learning
  - sports medicine
  - Olympic
  - elite athletes
  - CatBoost
  - XGBoost
  - LightGBM
  - SHAP
  - nested cross-validation
